    "confidence": 0.9,
    "explanation": "Both parties: this dispute is about the 5.00 SGD no-show cancellation fee charged to the rider at 08:19:14 on trip TRP-05057. The rider says the driver waited at the wrong block; the driver says he waited more than 10 minutes at the pickup and the rider never came. The record decides it for the rider.\n\nThe no-show policy's arrival test requires the trip record's arrival event to be corroborated by the GPS trace within the arrival radius, which is 50 m for a STANDARD pickup zone (POL-NS-21). It is not corroborated. The driver's own device trace (EV-GPS-05057) puts the vehicle no closer than 476.59 m from Block 251 anywhere in the 120-second window around the marked 08:06:50 arrival, and the vehicle then sits stationary roughly 650 m away from 08:06:50 through 08:18:50. The nearest fix reports an 8 m horizontal accuracy, well inside the 25 m accuracy filter, so this is not a bad reading. The driver's own chat message at 08:07:10 reads 'I reach already at Blk 215 carpark', while the booking label and the rider's 08:11:30 message put the meeting point at Block 251 (EV-CHAT-05057). The driver's later message, 'I'm at the pickup point waiting already', is a bare assertion his own trace contradicts. The driver was never at the pickup.\n\nBecause the driver never reached the pickup location, he failed to arrive by the scheduled 08:10:00 plus 5 minutes, i.e. by 08:15:00. Under POL-NS-24 the rider may cancel at no charge and any fee charged is refunded in full. The 5.00 SGD charged at 08:19:14 must therefore be returned to the rider: FULL_REFUND of the whole contested 5.00 SGD, with no driver compensation.\n\nOn the driver's surviving points: I accept that the POL-NS-23 contact obligation is met (a driver message at 08:07:10 and an in-app call at 08:15:20, both before the 08:19:10 cancellation), but POL-NS-23 is not the fee's foundation and does not save it. POL-NS-22 would transfer the fee to the driver only 'where the fee stands'; it does not stand here, so the claim for DRIVER_COMPENSATION at 5.00 SGD is rejected, as is the argument that the record's own arrived_by_deadline check settles the matter: that check is computed from the driver's arrival tap, and a tap a party sets records only that he set it, whereas the arrival test requires the tap to be corroborated by the trace. The free-wait timers (expiry 08:15:00, cancellation 08:19:10) are taken as correct but are outweighed, because they presuppose a driver waiting at the pickup, and the driver was not there. The absent traffic advisory (EV-ADVIS-05057-01, weight 0.0, MISSING_ARTIFACT) carries no fact and is needed by no rule, so no POL-GEN-26 escalation arises.\n\nNo referral fires. The fee charged, 5.00 SGD, matches the policy fee, so POL-NS-22's mis-stated-amount referral is not engaged; POL-NS-24's 5.00 SGD goodwill credit requires that the driver also failed to attempt contact, and he did attempt it; and POL-NS-25's repeat no-show flag counts only where the fee stands, which it does not.\n\nThe confidence is capped by the deciding fact's carriers, all at weight 1.0 (the GPS trace, the chat log and the trip record). The contested amount is 5.00 SGD, below POL-GEN-22's 10.00 SGD band, and neither profile carries a fraud flag, so under POL-GEN-22 and POL-NS-26 the AI ruling is final."
  },
  "discarded_claims": []
}

{
