    "explanation": "The 5.00 SGD no-show fee charged at 08:19:14 is refunded to you in full. Both parties agree, and I find, that the driver's contact obligation under POL-NS-23 was met — he sent an in-app message at 08:07:10 and placed an in-app call at 08:15:20, both before the 08:19:10 cancellation — so POL-NS-23 is not a refund ground. The refund rests on POL-NS-24 instead: the driver never arrived at the pickup location.\n\nThe policy's own arrival test (POL-NS-21) asks whether the trip record's arrival event is corroborated by the GPS trace within 50 m for a STANDARD pickup. The marked arrival is 08:06:50, but the nearest fix inside the 120 s window is index 18 at 08:04:50, 476.59 m away, and it reports an accuracy of 8.0 m — inside the 25 m filter, so this is not the product of a bad fix. From 08:06:50 to 08:18:50 every fix is stationary at roughly 650 m from Block 251, Hougang Avenue 3. An arrival tap is a status the driver sets; it records only that he pressed it, and the trace does not support it. On POL-NS-24 the driver failed to arrive at the pickup location by the scheduled pickup time (08:10) plus 5 minutes (08:15), and the fee charged is therefore refunded in full — 5.00 SGD.\n\nThe driver's points do not save the fee. The free-wait arithmetic (wait runs from scheduled_at 08:10, expires 08:15:00, cancellation 08:19:10) is correct, but a free wait is a wait at the pickup, and the arrival it presupposes is not made out; the record's arrived_by_deadline check reads that same uncorroborated button press. The stationary trace (25 fixes at speed 0) shows the vehicle standing still — standing still about 650 m from the pickup, not at it. The driver's own 08:07:10 message, 'I reach already at Blk 215 carpark', places him at a different block from the booking's Block 251, which the rider's 08:11:30 message and the pickup label confirm. POL-NS-22's fee condition is not satisfied, so the request for DRIVER_COMPENSATION at 5.00 SGD fails, and POL-GEN-03's NO_ACTION does not apply because the rider's claim is supported.\n\nNo referral is added. POL-NS-24's 5.00 SGD goodwill credit is due only where the driver also failed to attempt contact, and contact was attempted. POL-NS-25's repeat no-show flag does not fire: the field it names (no_show_cancellations_30d) is not on this profile, and the fee does not stand in any event. POL-NS-22's fee-amount referral is not engaged because the ledger charges exactly the 5.00 SGD policy fee. EV-ADVIS-05057-01 is a MISSING artifact of weight 0.0 and carries no fact; no no-show clause needs a traffic record, so POL-GEN-26 is not engaged.\n\nNo escalation is available: the amount contested is 5.00 SGD, below POL-GEN-22's 10.00 SGD band, there is no safety flag, and neither profile carries a fraud flag, so POL-GEN-22 and POL-NS-26 leave the decision to me. My confidence is 0.9, and the finding that the driver was not at the pickup is carried independently by the GPS trace (weight 1.0) and by the driver's own contemporaneous chat message (weight 1.0)."
